 everything gets more secure after superhuman LLM hackers, because the commoditization of intelligence favors defenders over attackers. Here’s why:</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/hosseeb/status/2080396229536800952?s=46&t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag">https://x.com/hosseeb/status/2080396229536800952?s=46&t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/saturday-assorted-links-571.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-571">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/hosseeb/status/2080396229536800952?s=46&amp;t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/hosseeb/status/2080396229536800952?s=46&amp;t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:38:10 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Simon Willison on The Incident]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/openai-cyberattack/">https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/openai-cyberattack/</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/saturday-assorted-links-571.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-571">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/openai-cyberattack/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/openai-cyberattack/</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:38:10 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[early AI fears were not about LLMs, and that makes a big difference]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1956138801060835329/kPG-TMDD_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Jon Stokes (@jon_stokes) on X</p><p>I’m going to take a crack at explaining this just a little, because it’s worth putting out there. The paperclip maximizer + related AI doom scenarios were mainly developed in a time when “AI” did not reduce to Large Language Models. The term was a lot wider and inherited a lot</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/jon_stokes/status/2080729236013187369">https://x.com/jon_stokes/status/2080729236013187369</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/saturday-assorted-links-571.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-571">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/jon_stokes/status/2080729236013187369</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/jon_stokes/status/2080729236013187369</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:38:10 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Critique of the new 76ers]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2025343539438387201/IHreYZmI_200x200.jpg"></p><p>databallr (@databallr) on X</p><p>There’s a lot of reasons to think the 2027 Sixers with LeBron could be most inefficient stacking of offensive talent in NBA history. It’s not just that the usage of the Rittenhouse 5 adds up to 140%. This alone is devastating. You are likely to get an offensive result that is</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/databallr/status/2080765040853123072">https://x.com/databallr/status/2080765040853123072</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/07/saturday-assorted-links-571.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=saturday-assorted-links-571">Saturday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/databallr/status/2080765040853123072</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/databallr/status/2080765040853123072</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:38:10 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Anthropic economic research futures allocating $200 million to RCTs]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2078660804074000384/cSg562UL_200x200.jpg"></p><p>D. Yanagizawa-Drott (@YanagizawaD) on X</p><p>Incredibly laudable move by @AnthropicAI: $200 million allocated to RCTs 🙌 @JPAL r